{
  "dom_id": "step-52943",
  "name": "Introduction",
  "problem": "To simplify an expression containing parentheses, we expand the parentheses and then collect like terms. \n\nFor example, let's simplify the following expression: \n\n$$\n3(x + 2) + 4x\n$$\n\n \n\nOur first step is to distribute the $3$ over each of the terms in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t3(x + 2) + 4x &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t3\\cdot x + 3\\cdot 2 + 4x &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t(3x) + (6) + 4x &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t3x +6 + 4x &\n\t}\n$$\n\nThe second and final step is to collect the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t3x + 6 + 4x &= \\\n\t\t(3x + 4x) + 6 &= \\\n\t\t7x + 6\n\t}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
